ut there's a lot  of other ways we could get to the night  king having a nice dragon if that was if  that was an important part of the story  I mean I don't want to ramble on about  this but what what purpose does it serve  so for every one that keeps asking when  I think about it I don't think it's  necessary and it sort of makes me wonder  about how different the end of the show  will be compared to the books when I say  different I think they're going to the  same place but I just don't I mean I  think this is a pretty far distance from  what's gonna happen in the books I could  be wrong a lot of people could be wrong  but it just doesn't seem likely  I won't completely hate on it since it  would probably still be fun to watch I'm  just not excited about and based on what  I just went over to be clear it's  definitely possible  this appointing when you've been super  into something you know you've been  reading watching and thinking about this  thing and it turns out differently than  what the consensus leading up to the end  was there are a lot more characters and  stories in the book so maybe some how  this works is a combination of things to  get to the same place at the end it's  hard to see but as  it would be to say that D and D are  incompetent and ruling everything that  hasn't really always been the case  they've done things I didn't like  and things that haven't made logical  sense but the show still is good at a  lot of things so freaking out like it  would be the end of the world is pretty  pointless to do I think the leak is  absolutely right no there's a lot of  stuff that's turning out to line up with  what's already out there though my view  is that some of the stuff just doesn't  add up  in that way it just goes to show how  leaks are not fun if it does turn out to  be a hundred percent right how has that  improved the experience of watching the  show for us I don't know about you guys  but I'm gonna wait until I see it to  believe it let me know